.TH SWIFTJ2K-CLI 1 "October 26, 2026" "12.1.0" "Swift Image Compression Suite"
.SH NAME
swiftj2k-cli \- lossless JPEG 2000 and HTJ2K encode, decode, transcode, inspect and validate for SwiftJ2K
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swiftj2k-cli
.RI [ options ] " command " [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The standalone executable of the SwiftJ2K library. It losslessly encodes
unsigned greyscale images (1 to 16 meaningful bits in 16-bit samples) to raw
JPEG 2000 Part 1 (j2k) or HTJ2K Part 15 (htj2k) codestreams, decodes such
codestreams (any tile grid, quality layers, code-block styles and progression
orders, reversible 5/3 wavelet, no quantisation), transcodes losslessly
between Part 1 and Part 15 in the wavelet coefficient domain without
materialising an intermediate pixel image, inspects and validates codestreams,
and reports the library's capabilities. Images enter and leave through the
NRRD interchange profile below; a shell pipe carries bytes, never shared
storage.
Build with Swift 6.2 or later (6.4 qualified) in Swift 6 language mode. Apple OS
minimum is 26.0. CLI hosts are macOS and Linux; consult the qualification
records for executed coverage.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B encode \-i IMAGE.nrrd \-o OUT.j2k [\-\-output-format j2k|htj2k] [\-\-levels N] [\-\-code-block WxH] [\-\-precision N]
Encode one NRRD greyscale image to a raw Part 1 (j2k, default) or Part 15
(htj2k) codestream: reversible 5/3 wavelet, one tile, one layer. \-\-levels
selects 0..32 decomposition levels (default min(5, floor(log2(min(width,
height))))), \-\-code-block a power-of-two size from 4 to 1024 whose area is
at most 4096 (default 64x64), and \-\-precision the meaningful bits when the
NRRD header carries no swiftj2k.meaningfulbits key (default 16). A key that
contradicts \-\-precision is a usage error.
.TP
.B decode \-i IN.j2k \-o IMAGE.nrrd
Decode a Part 1 or HTJ2K codestream to the NRRD profile with little-endian
samples and the codestream's meaningful bits recorded in the header key.
.TP
.B transcode \-i IN.j2k \-o OUT.j2c [\-\-input-format j2k|htj2k] [\-\-output-format j2k|htj2k] [\-\-levels N] [\-\-code-block WxH]
Losslessly transcode between Part 1 (j2k) and Part 15 (htj2k) codestreams in
the wavelet coefficient domain without allocating an intermediate pixel image
or writing temporary image files. Source decomposition levels are preserved by
default; requesting a different \-\-levels count is rejected with exit 4.
.TP
.B inspect \-i IN.j2k [\-\-json]
Report geometry, precision and format from the headers without decoding
samples; output on stdout as text or one JSON document.
.TP
.B validate \-i IN.j2k [\-\-json]
Fully decode in memory and report success or the defined failure; no output
file is written.
.TP
.B capabilities [\-\-json]
Report actual library encode/decode/inspect/transcode support. JSON is one
document on stdout.
.TP
.B help [command]
Show global or command-specific help. No arguments also show global help.
.TP
.B version
Show the development version.
.SH INPUT AND OUTPUT OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-input PATH
Input file, or \- for standard input, which is read completely first.
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output PATH
Final output file, or \- for binary standard output. A file is written to a
sibling temporary file and renamed into place; an existing file is refused
(exit 6) unless \-\-overwrite is given; nothing partial remains after a
failure. Binary standard output cannot be rolled back and a closed pipe is
reported as exit 6.
.TP
.B \-\-input-format j2k|htj2k|nrrd, \-\-output-format j2k|htj2k|nrrd
Declare formats; the declaration is checked against the bytes and a mismatch
is exit 4. Without a declaration the format is detected from the bytes only,
never from a filename.
.TP
.B \-\-overwrite
Permit replacing an existing output file.
.TP
.B \-\-json
For inspect and validate, a JSON document on stdout. For encode, decode and
transcode, a JSON report on stderr so that binary stdout stays clean.
.SH LIMIT AND POLICY OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-mode lossless
The only mode; near-lossless, lossy and \-\-max-error return 4.
.TP
.B \-\-backend scalar
The only backend; any other name returns 4.
.TP
.B \-\-copy-policy require-sharing|allow-copy
Accepted; neither policy copies on this path.
.TP
.B \-\-threads N, \-\-max-memory BYTES, \-\-timeout SECONDS
Worker limit 1..8, admission budget in bytes for input, output and workspace,
and the operation deadline (exit 5 when exceeded).
.SH NRRD PROFILE
Attached header ending in an empty line, magic NRRD0001 to NRRD0005, fields
type: uint16, dimension: 2, sizes: W H, encoding: raw and endian: little or
big. The key swiftj2k.meaningfulbits:=N (1..16) records the declared
precision; decode always writes it. Detached data files, line or byte skips,
block sizes, other types, dimensions and encodings are refused (exit 4);
a data length other than W*H*2 bytes is malformed (exit 3). Comments are
ignored. This is the CLI-04 interchange profile of the suite contract, not a
private format.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help, including after a command.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the development version.
.TP
.B \-v, \-vv, \-vvv, \-vvvv, \-vvvvv
Increase diagnostic verbosity, up to 5.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose LEVEL, \-\-verbose=LEVEL
Set level to 1 through 5, or + through +++++. Bare verbose increments once.
.TP
.B \-verbose: LEVEL, \-verbose:LEVEL
Equivalent explicit verbosity spelling; bare \-verbose increments once.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Suppress optional diagnostics; errors remain visible. Conflicts with
verbosity.
.SH DIAGNOSTIC LEVELS
Default 0 reports errors only. Levels are cumulative:
1 summary; 2 stages; 3 capability/configuration details; 4 elapsed timing;
5 bounded trace. Invalid levels or totals above 5 return 2.
Explicit levels set and repeated flags increment in argument order.
Diagnostics use stderr. Requested help/version/capability/inspection data uses
stdout. No payload bytes, metadata, raw addresses or input/output paths are
logged.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 2 invalid usage or argument; 3 malformed input; 4 unsupported
format, feature, layout or backend; 5 resource limit or deadline; 6 I/O or
storage failure, including an existing output without \-\-overwrite and a
closed pipe; 7 internal failure; 130 interrupted by SIGINT, with nothing
published.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
swiftj2k-cli encode \-i slice.nrrd \-o slice.j2k \-\-precision 12
swiftj2k-cli encode \-i slice.nrrd \-o slice.j2c \-\-output-format htj2k \-\-precision 12
swiftj2k-cli decode \-i slice.j2k \-o slice.nrrd \-\-overwrite
swiftj2k-cli transcode \-i source.j2k \-\-input-format j2k \-\-output-format htj2k \-\-mode lossless \-o converted.j2c
swiftj2k-cli transcode \-i converted.j2c \-\-input-format htj2k \-\-output-format j2k \-\-mode lossless \-o restored.j2k
swiftj2k-cli decode \-i \- \-o \- < slice.j2k | swiftj2k-cli encode \-i \- \-\-input-format nrrd \-o out.j2k
swiftj2k-cli inspect \-i slice.j2k \-\-json
swiftj2k-cli validate \-i slice.j2k
swiftj2k-cli capabilities \-\-json \-vv
.fi
.SH INSTALLATION
Scripts/install-cli.sh installs or updates the executable and this page
together.
Use \-\-prefix for an absolute prefix (default /usr/local), \-\-destdir or
DESTDIR
for staging, and \-\-binary for a prebuilt binary matching VERSION.
Files are PREFIX/bin/swiftj2k-cli and PREFIX/share/man/man1/swiftj2k-cli.1.
For custom prefixes use man \-M PREFIX/share/man swiftj2k-cli, or configure
MANPATH.
No index refresh is needed for direct lookup; no sudo runs automatically.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR man (1)
.PP
CLI.md, TRANSCODING.md and Documentation/MILESTONE6.md in the SwiftJ2K repository.
